<title>GERMANY: German state Bavaria CPI -0.1 mth/mth,up 1.3 yr/yr.</title>
<headline>German state Bavaria CPI -0.1 mth/mth,up 1.3 yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state statistics office in the German state of Bavaria reported the following consumer price changes for the month to mid-August.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		August		July</p>
<p>    Month/month (pct change)  -0.1		  +0.4</p>
<p>    Year/year		     +1.3		  +1.3</p>
<p>NOTE - This data is combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary figure for the whole of west Germany. Bavaria was the last of the four to report its August data.  </p>
<p>Bavaria gave the following breakdown of the cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr    Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.1	+1.3     114.5</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.2	+2.8     126.4</p>
<p> Household energy			  -1.5	+14.2    86.6</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  +0.2	+1.0     128.4</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  -0.2	+1.6     115.5</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods unch	+0.7     109.7</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   -0.6	+0.6     108.4</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   +0.2	+1.0     106.7</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1	+2.1     114.0</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   unch	+0.9     109.3</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
